# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neon Postgres
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both strings point at the SAME database. They differ only in which Neon
# endpoint host they resolve to. Using the wrong one is a real bug:
#
#   DATABASE_URL         -> POOLED  (host contains "-pooler")
#                           PgBouncer in transaction mode. Use for the web app,
#                           the worker's normal query path, and anything that
#                           opens many short-lived connections. Neon's compute
#                           can scale to zero behind it.
#
#   DATABASE_URL_DIRECT  -> DIRECT  (host WITHOUT "-pooler")
#                           A real Postgres connection. Required for anything
#                           that needs session state: drizzle-kit migrations,
#                           `drizzle-kit studio`, COPY, CREATE EXTENSION,
#                           advisory locks. Migrations WILL fail on the pooled
#                           string.
#
# Where to find them in the Neon console:
#   1. https://console.neon.tech -> select your project
#   2. Dashboard -> "Connection string" panel (or Project settings -> Connect)
#   3. Choose branch = production (or your dev branch), database, and role
#   4. Toggle "Connection pooling":
#        ON  -> copy into DATABASE_URL         (host: ep-xxx-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech)
#        OFF -> copy into DATABASE_URL_DIRECT  (host: ep-xxx.<region>.aws.neon.tech)
#   5. Neon hands you `?sslmode=require`. Change it to `?sslmode=verify-full`
#      on both, as below. node-postgres already treats `require` as
#      `verify-full`, and warns that it will stop doing so in pg v9; saying
#      `verify-full` outright is identical today and immune to that change.
#      Neon rejects unencrypted connections either way.
#
# The password is only shown once at role creation; use "Reset password" on the
# role if you lose it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-xxxx-pooler.ap-southeast-1.aws.neon.tech/nse_signals?sslmode=verify-full"
DATABASE_URL_DIRECT="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-xxxx.ap-southeast-1.aws.neon.tech/nse_signals?sslmode=verify-full"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neon API (test-branch automation only — not needed to run the app)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The schema test suite creates a throwaway Neon branch, migrates it, asserts
# against it, and deletes it. That needs an API key:
#   1. https://console.neon.tech -> Account settings -> API keys
#   2. "Create new API key", copy it (shown once)
# An account-scoped key can reach every project on the account; prefer an
# org- or project-scoped key if one is available to you.
#
# Leave this unset and the schema tests skip rather than fail.
NEON_API_KEY=""
# Project the test branches are created in. Neon console -> Project settings ->
# General -> "Project ID", or `GET /api/v2/projects?org_id=<org>`.
NEON_PROJECT_ID=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fyers API v3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create an app at https://fyers.in/web/api-dashboard/user-apps
#   - Redirect URI must match FYERS_REDIRECT_URI below exactly.
#   - "Market Data" permission is required for history and quotes.
#   - Since 1 Apr 2026 SEBI requires a separate, IP-whitelisted app for ORDER
#     placement. A data-only app needs no static IP.
FYERS_APP_ID=""            # e.g. SPXXXXE7-100
FYERS_SECRET_KEY=""        # app secret; never commit
FYERS_REDIRECT_URI="https://trade.fyers.in/api-login/redirect-uri/index.html"

# Access token. Expires daily — the refresh-token flow was discontinued on
# 1 Apr 2026 and daily 2FA is now mandatory.
#
# A FALLBACK, not the normal path. When the three fields below are set, the
# worker mints a token every morning and stores it in the `provider_credentials`
# table, and both the worker and the web app read it from there. This value is
# used only when no stored credential is usable — a fresh checkout, or a
# deliberate choice to log in by hand (`pnpm fyers:login`).
FYERS_ACCESS_TOKEN=""

# Unattended daily re-login. Set all three and the token refreshes on its own at
# 08:30 IST; leave all three blank to log in by hand every day. Setting only
# some of them is an error the worker reports at startup rather than a partial
# configuration that silently never refreshes.
#
# Uses UNDOCUMENTED Fyers endpoints that may break without notice; a failure is
# logged loudly and asks you to log in by hand rather than retrying blindly.
#
# THESE ARE ACCOUNT-LEVEL SECRETS. FYERS_TOTP_SECRET is the same 2FA seed that
# protects your brokerage login, including the order-placing side this app
# deliberately has nothing to do with. Give them ONLY to the worker, on a host
# you control. Never put them on a serverless deploy: a deployed web app needs
# the minted token and nothing more, and that token dies within the day and can
# only read market data.
FYERS_ID=""                # your FYERS login ID, e.g. XK12345
FYERS_TOTP_SECRET=""       # base32 secret from 2FA setup
FYERS_PIN=""               # 4-digit login PIN

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (first-party, multi-user — docs/planning/authentication-plan.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   AUTH_SESSION_SECRET   32+ random bytes; signs the session cookie. REQUIRED in prod.
#   AUTH_ALLOW_SIGNUP     "false" closes public sign-up. Default: open.
#   AUTH_BASE_URL         base URL used in email links. Default: https://equitywise.io (prod).
#
# Transactional email (verification + password reset) via Resend. With no key,
# links are printed to the server log — fine for local dev.
#   RESEND_API_KEY        Resend API key (re_...). REQUIRED for real email delivery.
#   AUTH_EMAIL_FROM       Sender. Default: "EquityWise Support <support@equitywise.io>".
#                         Must be an address on the Resend-verified domain.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AUTH_SESSION_SECRET=""
AUTH_ALLOW_SIGNUP="true"
RESEND_API_KEY=""
AUTH_EMAIL_FROM="EquityWise Support <support@equitywise.io>"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploying on the VPS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS FILE IS NOT DEPLOYED. `.env` is gitignored. On the VPS the real .env
# lives outside the git checkout, root-owned and `chmod 600`; `next.config.ts`
# dotenv-loads the repo-root path. Both processes run under PM2 (see the
# Production Hosting & VPS Migration Plan for the full runbook).
#
# The web app (apps/web) needs exactly TWO values, and no secret beyond them:
#
#   DATABASE_URL                        the POOLED database string
#   FYERS_APP_ID                        live-quote routes only
#
# FYERS_ACCESS_TOKEN is NOT in that list, and deliberately so. The worker mints
# a token each morning into `provider_credentials`; the web app reads it from
# there.
#
# `next build` does NOT fail when the Clerk keys are absent. `clerkMiddleware`
# throws instead, on every request, so the whole site answers 500 — /sign-in
# included, because the middleware runs before it. That is the error you are
# reading if a running app serves nothing.
#
# Keep the web app's environment to those four values. DATABASE_URL_DIRECT,
# FYERS_SECRET_KEY, FYERS_ID, FYERS_TOTP_SECRET, FYERS_PIN and NEON_API_KEY
# belong ONLY to the worker (and a developer machine): migrations, the OAuth
# handshake, the daily re-login and the test-branch automation run there. An
# unused secret is still a secret at risk, and the TOTP seed and PIN are
# account-level — see the Fyers section above.
#
#   - /api/fyers/connect and /callback (the Fyers OAuth handshake) write the new token into
#     .fyers-token.json and this repo's .env — which the VPS filesystem allows.
#     With the worker's daily refresh running, nothing here needs doing at all.
#   - apps/worker runs under PM2 on the same VPS. It is what writes new candles,
#     signals and paper trades and refreshes the token; without it the site
#     serves whatever it last stored.
